BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:46th Annual Waters Farm Days
DTSTART:20261017T000000
DTEND:20261018T000000
DTSTAMP:20261017T144006Z
UID:4cccc58407619ff63b03be08724fbe@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Visit Waters Farm on October 17 and 18 for a family-oriented w
 eekend full of fun activities and educational experiences. In addition to 
 the many activities and vendors you look forward to seeing each year\, the
 re are new activities and performances scheduled for the 46th Annual Farm 
 Days celebration in West Sutton. The Providence Brigade Band\, a 19th cent
 ury brass band\, will offer two performances each day at 11:00 a.m. and 2:
 00 p.m. Band members dress in military uniforms of the period and play wit
 h Civil War era instruments. The band has performed throughout southeaster
 n New England as well as Gettysburg PA. Additional music will be provided 
 by Cruisin’ Bruce Palmer. We will also welcome back the Witches of Sutto
 n for a Sunday afternoon performance. The Sutton Agricultural Trust is pla
 nning a Farmer Fitness Competition. More information on this event will fo
 llow. Also sponsored by the Sutton AG Trust\, the Animal Showcase will inc
 lude 4-H animals\, goats\, small farm animals\, cattle projects\, and Ange
 l Hair Alpacas. Other animal exhibitors will include horses\, donkeys\, mu
 les\, working teams of oxen\, pet rescues and dog agility demonstrations. 
 The Ken Ethier Memorial Antique Tractor Show features the Chapter 18 Inter
 national Harvester Club and other enthusiasts from New England\, who will 
 be displaying and demonstrating their antique tractors\, implements\, and 
 doodlebugs. The farm also features Antique Tractor Pulls\, with registrati
 on beginning at 9:00 a.m. and pulling beginning at 10:00 a.m. and ending w
 hen the last tractor pulls the heaviest load over the finish line. Kiddie 
 pedal tractor pulls will be held\, track permitting\, during lunch breaks 
 at the pull. Come and cheer them on! The Sten Brote Memorial Engine Show h
 onors decades of collecting\, restoring\, and honoring antique engines. On
  Sunday\, come and view all of the vehicles participating in the Bruce Nic
 hols Memorial Car Show\, located in the upper field. Did you know that Ste
 phen Waters\, builder of the original 1757 portion of the farmhouse\, and 
 all three of his brothers served in the Revolutionary War? Learn about the
 ir service\, Waters family history\, and speak with our resident Waters ge
 nealogist in the Darling Barn. You may also view local history presented b
 y the Sutton Historical Society. There will be a number of craft vendors a
 nd food vendors located throughout the farm property\, including Waters Fa
 rm Famous Apple Crisp\, served plain\, with ice cream or homemade caramel 
 sauce. Delicious! Stop in at the Peddler’s Shop for Waters Farm related 
 clothing and gifts. Visit the Darling Barn to view a Halloween Village dis
 play\, courtesy of Doug Matthews. Demonstrations from years past include o
 ur working Blacksmith Shop\, Maple Sugar House\, and Shingle Mill\, plus a
 n antique hammer mill processing grain near the Shingle Mill. Costumed int
 erpreters will cook on the restored hearth in the Waters Farmhouse and giv
 e tours of the family home. Children’s activities take place on both day
 s. Enjoy games\, contests\, barrel train rides\, inflatables\, and bottle 
 rockets. The Sutton Robotic Team and Scouts will also be onsite. Wagon rid
 es will be provided by our neighbor\, Whittier Farms. Representatives from
  the Sutton Food Pantry will be collecting donations of shelf stable food 
 and supplies in the parking lot. There is so much to see and do at the 46t
 h Annual Farm Days at historic Waters Farm. We hope to see you there! Sour
 ces: Discover Central Massachusetts Event page: https://www.discovercentra
 lma.org/event/46th-annual-waters-farm-days/30889/\n\nEvents Near Me: withi
 n 30 miles of Northborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback from mass
 achusetts-events.ics\nSource page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event
 /46th-annual-waters-farm-days/30889/
LOCATION:Waters Farm Preservation\, Inc.\, 25 Waters Road mailing address:
  4 Uxbridge Rd\, Sutton\, MA\, 01590
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/46th-annual-waters-farm-days/3
 0889/
END:VEVENT
