BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Intergenerational Game of Telephone
DTSTART:20261017T000000
DTEND:20261017T000000
DTSTAMP:20261017T144006Z
UID:d825f6d2d1886d942df79ce868e557@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Meet up-and-coming scientists and learn about questions at the
  forefront of research today in this series of short talks. Speaker: Sasha
  Post Graduate Student - Dept. of Human Evolutionary Biology Let’s play 
 a game of telephone! One player whispers a message to the next. The catch?
  The next player hasn’t even been born yet. Over millions of years\, mam
 mals have devised strategies for playing “intergenerational telephone\,
 ” sharing messages about the environment with their developing offspring
 . Researchers increasingly recognize the profound impact of these messages
  on human health. Join Harvard scientist Sasha Post as he breaks down the 
 strategies humans use to play\, why these strategies evolved\, and how we 
 can change the game to improve public health. Recommended for ages 10 and 
 up. Regular museum admission rates apply. Presented by the Harvard Museum 
 of Natural History and Harvard Museums of Science & Culture LEARN MORE / G
 ET TICKETS Sources: Meet Boston Event page: https://www.meetboston.com/eve
 nt/an-intergenerational-game-of-telephone/93638/\n\nEvents Near Me: within
  30 miles of Northborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback from massa
 chusetts-events.ics\nSource page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/an-inte
 rgenerational-game-of-telephone/93638/
LOCATION:Harvard Museum of Natural History\, Harvard Museum of Natural His
 tory 26 Oxford Street Classroom B\, Third Floor\, Cambridge\, MA\, 02138
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/an-intergenerational-game-of-telephon
 e/93638/
END:VEVENT
