SUMMARY:Carved Images: Relief Printmaking
DTSTART:20261020T000000
DTEND:20261201T000000
DTSTAMP:20261017T144006Z
UID:34628b748cc48f449127d00ec524b4@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Course Description: Relief is the oldest printmaking technique
  in the world\, with its origins dating back to at least 200 CE in China. 
 While materials and tools have evolved\, the general technique of carving 
 away negative space to create a raised image has remained the same. Studen
 ts will learn to work with basic techniques of making print blocks using v
 arious wood types and other types of substrates like linoleum. Once the ca
 rving or construction of the block is complete\, students will learn how t
 o effectively ink up and print their block on paper by hand printing and u
 sing an etching press. Students Should Bring: printmaking paper\, x-acto k
 nives\, gloves Dates: Weekly from October 20 - December 1 Meets: Tuesdays 
 from 6:00 PM to 9:00 PM Sources: Discover Central Massachusetts Event page
 : https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/carved-images%3a-relief-printmak
 ing/31042/\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 miles of Northborough\, MA 01532\n
 Discovery: Local fallback from massachusetts-events.ics\nSource page: http
 s://www.discovercentralma.org/event/carved-images%3a-relief-printmaking/31
 042/
LOCATION:Worcester Center for Crafts\, 25 Sagamore Rd.\, Worcester\, MA\, 
 01605
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/carved-images%3a-relief-printm
 aking/31042/
END:VEVENT
