BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Digital Photography 2
DTSTART:20261020T000000
DTEND:20261201T000000
DTSTAMP:20261017T144006Z
UID:4b40d01034cf68e1fd800e11d6841b@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Do you have some camera experience and are looking to grow as 
 a photographer? Look no further! Digital Photo 2 is for you! Take the next
  steps with your understanding of digital photography with "Digital Photog
 raphy II." In this course\, you will improve your use of manual settings w
 hile learning how to "see" when looking through the viewfinder of your cam
 era. Explore some of the many different types of photography such as portr
 ait\, landscape\, still life\, and abstraction\, as you become more confid
 ent with your choices of composition and visual content. You will improve 
 your digital workflow and learn basic photo editing skills using Adobe Pho
 toshop. Print-quality images will be created as students learn the basic s
 teps of preparing an image print. Students should be familiar with the bas
 ics of photography as well as the controls and functions of their digital 
 camera and will be assigned an iMac computer workstation accessible during
  class time. Perfect for those who have taken "Intro to Photography" or wa
 nt to improve their beginner skills in digital photography. It is requeste
 d all students provide a new\, unused memory card for their camera before 
 interfacing with computers in the lab. Materials fee will support ink and 
 paper for up to five test prints per/student Dates: Weekly from October 20
  - December 1 Meets: Tuesday from 6:30 PM - 9:30 PM Sources: Discover Cent
 ral Massachusetts Event page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/intr
 oduction-to-digital-photography-2/31043/\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 mile
 s of Northborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback from massachusetts
 -events.ics\nSource page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/introduc
 tion-to-digital-photography-2/31043/
LOCATION:Worcester Center for Crafts\, 25 Sagamore Rd.\, Worcester\, MA\, 
 01605
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/introduction-to-digital-photog
 raphy-2/31043/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Latinx Civil Wars
DTSTART:20261020T000000
DTEND:20261020T000000
DTSTAMP:20261017T144006Z
UID:4cebe577fce2964d88fa54ce86a47d@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Jesse Alemán reflects on his 2026 book\, Latinx Civil Wars\, 
 the first book-length study of US Latinx writings about the Civil War by M
 exican American and Cuban American Union and Confederate combatants and sy
 mpathizers. His research\, much of it done at the American Antiquarian Soc
 iety\, drew on a rich archive of unpublished personal letters and manuscri
 pts in Spanish and English\, official Union and Confederate records and di
 spatches\, and published essays\, poems\, manifestos\, news articles\, mem
 oirs\, autobiographies\, and novels. In this hybrid talk\, Alemán shows h
 ow the formation of nineteenth-century Latinx identity was entangled with 
 slavery\, independence\, racialization\, and rebellion—revealing Latinid
 ad as a product not of unity but of conflict and contradiction. This progr
 am will be held in person and livestreamed. Register for both options here
 . Jesse Alemán is a professor of English and Presidential Teaching Fellow
  at the University of New Mexico\, where he teaches nineteenth-century Ame
 rican and US Latinx literary and cultural histories. He is the author of L
 atinx Civil Wars (New York University Press\, 2026)\, the editor of The Wo
 man in Battle: The Civil War Narrative of Loreta Janeta Velázquez \, and 
 the co-editor with Rodrigo Lazo of The Latino Nineteenth Century . Alemán
  was the Mellon Distinguished Scholar in Residence at AAS in 2023-2024. He
  was elected to membership in April 2012. Sources: Discover Central Massac
 husetts Event page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/latinx-civil-w
 ars/30656/\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 miles of Northborough\, MA 01532\n
 Discovery: Local fallback from massachusetts-events.ics\nSource page: http
 s://www.discovercentralma.org/event/latinx-civil-wars/30656/
LOCATION:American Antiquarian Society\, 185 Salisbury St.\, Worcester\, MA
 \, 01609
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/latinx-civil-wars/30656/
END:VEVENT
