BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Proper Fit: Women at Work in a City of Corsets
DTSTART:20261021T000000
DTEND:20261021T000000
DTSTAMP:20261017T144006Z
UID:ae4611dedee5f37fefe08763e0c153@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Worcester Public Library presents a book talk by Anne Marie Mu
 rphy on her new book A Proper Fit: Women at Work in a City of Corsets . Di
 scover a city full of women making corsets: Worcester\, Massachusetts from
  1860 to 1980. The city hosted over 120 corset-making businesses and half 
 of them were owned by women. This book tells the stories of many of those 
 female business owners\, how they got into the business\, how they learned
  to make this challenging garment\, and how they self-supported in the cit
 y for over a century\, as small shop "corsetieres" and forewomen and trave
 ling saleswomen and even as a factory owner. Banx Room Register https://my
 wpl.libnet.info/event/16764148 Sources: Discover Central Massachusetts Eve
 nt page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/a-proper-fit%3a-women-at-
 work-in-a-city-of-corsets/30611/\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 miles of Nor
 thborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback from massachusetts-events.
 ics\nSource page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/a-proper-fit%3a-
 women-at-work-in-a-city-of-corsets/30611/
LOCATION:Worcester Public Library\, 3 Salem St.\, Worcester\, MA\, 01608
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/a-proper-fit%3a-women-at-work-
 in-a-city-of-corsets/30611/
END:VEVENT
