BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Many Lives of Theban Tomb 16
DTSTART:20261021T000000
DTEND:20261021T000000
DTSTAMP:20261017T144006Z
UID:d548f48c52fe0f232879b93212ae72@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:The ancient Egyptian tomb known as Theban Tomb 16 dates to the
  reign of Ramesses II in the Nineteenth Dynasty of the New Kingdom (around
  1250 BCE). Originally\, it served as the burial place of a priest named P
 anehsy and his wife\, Tarenu\, a chantress. Long after their lifetimes\, t
 he tomb remained an important resting place and was reused for more than a
  thousand years by members of the Theban elite. By the late-nineteenth or 
 early-twentieth twentieth century\, the tomb had been looted\, and it suff
 ered further plundering in the 1970s. Since 2008\, however\, a team from t
 he University of Memphis has been working to document and conserve both th
 e tomb and its many secondary burials. In this program\, Egyptologist Suza
 nne Onstine will present the latest research on the tomb’s beautifully p
 ainted plaster scenes\, exploring what they reveal about life in ancient E
 gypt as well as funerary culture during the first millennium BCE. Free adm
 ission. Free event parking is available with registration. Register by Oct
 ober 20 to receive parking registration instructions. Presented by the Har
 vard Museum of the Ancient Near East and the Harvard Museums of Science an
 d Culture. LEARN MORE Sources: Meet Boston Event page: https://www.meetbos
 ton.com/event/the-many-lives-of-theban-tomb-16/93483/\n\nEvents Near Me: w
 ithin 30 miles of Northborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback from 
 massachusetts-events.ics\nSource page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/th
 e-many-lives-of-theban-tomb-16/93483/
LOCATION:Geological Lecture Hall\, Geological Lecture Hall 24 Oxford Stree
 t\, Cambridge\, MA\, 02138
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/the-many-lives-of-theban-tomb-16/9348
 3/
END:VEVENT
